        "id": 1899961
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-11T18:03:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Exactly, I didn\u0027t want to add additional mount_info struct members indicating whether the dir was created or opened, since it could be derived from the value of sb-\u003es_stack_depth. I\u0027m not sure if different stacking fs could break it because the super block that is created in incfs_mount_fs() and freed in incfs_kill_sb() is owned by the incr_fs, and on other fs should mess with it. But I can see if I can make it more explicit so there is no confusion.",
